_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786663347051788001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e51da71e-90a0-4cf4-91e7-0c8ebdfa709c","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"cef7-7ac5-18e6-41a3"},{"link_uuid":"4340da73-d4ef-4fe9-8f2d-52e0d2936525","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7315-6af1-6b2b-458f"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nAGENTS.md's \"Module-size policy (when editing rebar itself)\" section prominently documents the 800-LOC module-size gate (`.github/module-size-limit.txt`) but says NOTHING about its sibling CI gate: the shrink-only C901 cyclomatic-complexity ratchet (`.github/complexity-baseline.json`, McCabe max-complexity 15, enforced by `scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` as part of `make lint`).\n\nThe ratchet fails the build whenever a function gains NEW debt or grows PAST its recorded per-symbol ceiling. This is exactly the failure mode of routine work like adding a CLI flag or a guard clause (added branches -> increased complexity), so an agent that adds a couple of flags to an existing command (e.g. create_cli/edit_cli) hits it predictably. Because it is a structural gate the behavioral test oracle cannot see, an implementer/orchestrator only discovers it at pre-flight, forcing an unplanned behavior-preserving extraction pass.\n\nDiscovered while implementing story cef7 (bridge_project/repos create+edit flags): the flag/guard additions pushed create_core (23>21), create_cli (26>22), edit_core (24>21) past ceiling and made edit_cli (16) new, failing `make lint` although the change was under the 800 LOC cap and lint/typecheck were otherwise clean.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a short paragraph to AGENTS.md's Module-size policy section (or an adjacent \"Structural gates\" note) surfacing the complexity ratchet next to the LOC cap: what it is, that it is part of `make lint`, that it is shrink-only (fails on new/increased debt, ceilings in `.github/complexity-baseline.json`, threshold 15 in pyproject `[tool.ruff.lint.mccabe]`), that the fix is behavior-preserving extraction (never bumping the baseline), and how to inspect it (`ruff check --select C901 <file>` / `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`). Cross-reference from the rebar-implement skill's 'ship the constraints the oracle cannot see' step so implementer briefs quote it alongside the module-size limit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AGENTS.md surfaces the C901 shrink-only complexity ratchet in/next to the Module-size policy section, naming the gate command, the baseline file, the threshold source, and the extraction-not-baseline-bump remedy.\n- [ ] The note explains it runs under `make lint` and blocks CI like the module-size gate.\n- [ ] A one-line pointer is added so a reader knows how to census offenders (`ruff check --select C901`).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"document the C901 shrink-only complexity ratchet alongside the module-size cap"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7315-6af1-6b2b-458f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"daab8509-fe2f-4195-9469-944f87ec7548","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3b78-de05-a125-418f","ticket_type":"task","title":"Surface the shrink-only C901 complexity ratchet in AGENTS.md alongside the module-size cap","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8789c003-da3d-496f-b1a0-f80c456efc5d","f94a839d-8430-4d3c-b5a0-587d145bed5a","e51da71e-90a0-4cf4-91e7-0c8ebdfa709c","00d26248-6a71-473f-a501-96a36fe85572","daab8509-fe2f-4195-9469-944f87ec7548","1eadb144-7b4f-4416-b409-e045a040f46e","4340da73-d4ef-4fe9-8f2d-52e0d2936525"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786664344269697533,"uuid":"3aa2c753-41bb-4e65-aa0b-49c2abbc8287"}